      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00003",
          "explanation": "Doctor actively attempted to use available records rather than relying only on family memory.",
          "quote": "我调取该患者在 CareLoop 联合医疗网络中已授权访问的既往病历"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00005",
          "explanation": "Workspace confirmed records were visible to the doctor.",
          "quote": "可见既往/CareLoop 中心医院记录 5 条"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor used the clinical workspace and incorporated available diagnosis/procedure context instead of fabricating missing laboratory or imaging results.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC2_workspace_grounding_for_incomplete_account",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00061",
          "explanation": "Doctor identified key preoperative-result categories needing review.",
          "quote": "血常规、凝血、心电图、心肺功能评估"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00137",
          "explanation": "Doctor gave the family specific questions to close the anesthesia and vital-sign decision loop.",
          "quote": "麻醉医生来过了吗？麻醉同意签了吗？"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor kept pending results and anesthesia clearance open until the inpatient team confirmed them and gave the family concrete questions to ask before transport.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC3_pending_results_and_preop_decision_loop",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00061",
          "explanation": "Doctor set the correct medication-execution rule during the preoperative period.",
          "quote": "所有药物现在都必须按病房医嘱执行"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00402",
          "explanation": "Doctor tied anticoagulant duration to the discharge order rather than family guesswork.",
          "quote": "必须按出院单上的天数吃完"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor repeatedly instructed the family not to self-administer or change antihypertensive, diabetes, anticoagulant, analgesic, or gastric-protection medications and to confirm timing/doses with the ward, pharmacy, or written discharge orders.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC4_medication_safety",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00424",
          "explanation": "Doctor covered several important home red flags and escalation routes.",
          "quote": "纱布很快湿透"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00424",
          "explanation": "Doctor included thrombotic/respiratory and infection-type emergency triggers.",
          "quote": "腿突然明显肿痛"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The plan covered bleeding, wound infection, fever, thrombosis, dyspnea/chest symptoms, and fall response, but it did not explicitly provide the required pulmonary-infection and pressure-ulcer prevention/red-flag action plan such as deep breathing/coughing, patting back, or scheduled turning for pressure prevention. This is a minor/moderate in-chain omission rather than a serious safety failure because multiple major red flags and escalation paths were still provided.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC5_postop_complication_and_red_flag_plan",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
